{
  "borough": "Waltham Forest",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development is unacceptable in principle as the\r\napplication site is located within 400m (10 minutes walking distance) to a preschool\r\ncontrary to Policy 51 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "The application as submitted has failed to provide specification details of the existing extraction system, the proposal also fails to demonstrate that odours from the extraction system would not unreasonably impact the above residential occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy 57 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "Due to insufficient detailing within the proposed/ existing plans and conflicting information within the supporting documentation the applicant has failed to demonstrate that there will be adequate provision for the storage, collection and disposal of refuse for the existing use, leading to potential adverse effects on the amenity of local residents contrary to Policy 57 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "Notwithstanding the first three points of refusal, the applicant is required to serve notice to all parties with a leasehold or freehold interest in the land 21 days prior to the submission of the application in accordance with article 13 of the Town and Country Planning Act (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015. The applicant failed to indicate that&nbsp;all&nbsp;leaseholders were served the applicable notice 21 days prior to the submission of the proposal."
  ],
